# Reactive State

The modular service is the source of truth. Renderer stores display snapshots
and push events.

- Fetch an initial snapshot before or while subscribing to domain pushes.
- Treat engine and model commands as fire-and-forget mutations.
- Do not populate durable state from mutation responses.
- Render engine lifecycle from `engines:state-changed`.
- Render operation progress from `engines:progress-changed` and
  `engines:progress-cleared`.
- Keep node, metrics, workloads, discovery, cluster, and error state in their
  own stores.

## Pending actions

`src/ui/stores/pending-actions.store.ts` is the only optimistic operation state
for engine and model commands.

- `fireCommand` in `src/ui/api/engine-api.ts` starts pending entries.
- Components may read pending entries but must not write them.
- Backend state, progress, and matching errors supersede optimistic state.
- Pending state is memory-only and must not survive reload.
- Entries are keyed by node and action so remote and local operations share the
  same mechanism.

Do not add per-component lifecycle or model loading flags.

## Backend-owned lifecycle preferences

Engine auto-start and lifecycle persistence are owned by
`nvpair-engine-manager`. PAIR sends commands and reflects reported state; it
must not maintain a second auto-start source of truth.
